.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1037 AM PDT Thu Oct 8 2026

Patchy fog and LIFR stratus lingers at the immediate coast with the
rest of the region remaining VFR through the daytime. A gentle to
moderate onshore pattern wind develops in the afternoon and
evening hours. This evening and tonight, the marine layer is
expected to rebuild and thicken as large scale ridging moves
eastwards, allowing for some improved inland expansion of the
stratus deck. Forecast confidence is moderate for stratus extent
and ceiling heights, but expect some inland development into the
North bay valleys, SF Bay, and Salinas Valley overnight. Stratus
begins to retreat back to the coastal regions Friday morning.

Vicinity of SFO... Moderate confidence for VFR conditions through
the TAF period with some scattered clouds possible late tonight.
Higher confidence in stratus impacts at OAK. Moderate west-northwest
winds will develop in the afternoon and evening hours, with light
winds overnight into the morning.

SFO Bridge Approach... Similar to SFO

Monterey Bay Terminals... Lingering fog and LIFR stratus is expected
to lift imminently at MRY but potentially persist through the
afternoon along the immediate coast. Otherwise VFR conditions remain
prevalent through the day with gentle to moderate northwest winds in
the afternoon hours. IFR-LIFR stratus develops this evening with
moderate confidence for fog, not expected to clear out until the TAF
period ends on Friday morning, or shortly thereafter.

