.MARINE...
(Today through Tuesday)
Issued at 907 AM PDT Thu Oct 8 2026

Moderate to fresh northwesterly breezes and moderate seas will
prevail today. Conditions deteriorate Friday and into the weekend
as northerly breezes increase to become strong to near gale across
the coastal waters, Monterey Bay, and through the Golden Gate
Gap. Gale force gusts are expected across the northern outer
waters and the coastal jet region of Point Reyes. These winds will
build rough to very rough seas. Long period southerly swell
arrives Friday, with long period northwesterly swell arriving
Sunday, creating a confused sea state.

